<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">1st Czechoslovak Army Corps</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1944–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as 1st Czechoslovak Army Corps in the USSR</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 1st Czechoslovak Army Corps was a Czechoslovak formation that fought alongside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, formed in 1944 from the brigade raised in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludvik-svoboda">Ludvík Svoboda</a>. It suffered heavy losses in the Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dukla-pass">Dukla Pass</a> in autumn 1944 and fought through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> until 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/1st-czechoslovak-army-corps.jpg" alt="1st Czechoslovak Army Corps" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ThecentreCZ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_1st_Czechoslovak_Army_Corps_in_USSR_(reverse).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
